findings.recommendation:
Make it impossible to ship silently rather than merely noisy:
```go
if cfg.AllowedOrigins == "" {
    if cfg.Storage != "memory" { // a real database means a real deployment
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("config: CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS обязателен при APP_STORAGE=%s", cfg.Storage)
    }
    log.Printf("config: CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS пуст — RequireSameOrigin сверяется с %s://<r.Host>", scheme)
}
if cfg.Storage != "memory" && !cfg.CookieSecure {
    return nil, errors.New("config: COOKIE_SECURE=true обязателен при APP_STORAGE != memory")
}
```
Drop the `&& !cfg.CookieSecure` conjunct from the warning so the empty-allowlist state is always reported. Add two table cases in internal/config asserting Load fails (or warns) for each combination, and set both values as real GitHub secrets before Wave 12.

Close the admin handle inside the cleanup, after the DROP, and stop discarding the error:
```go
t.Cleanup(func() {
    if _, err := admin.Exec("DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS " + dbName); err != nil {
        t.Errorf("drop %s: %v", dbName, err)
    }
    admin.Close()
})
```
and delete the `defer admin.Close()` on line 54. Then drop the seven stray `migration_race_*` databases on poshivon_db.

